Done. `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` are written in the step 3 folder and verified with forward passes.

**→ Result.** Evidence goes from **14/32 to 27/32** correct. On held-out messages I wrote: **16/20** new eligibility questions route to account_security. Of 40 near-confusers (card delivery abroad, card acceptance, currencies, kids' cards), **3 change**, and 2 of those are arguably correct anyway. Of 253 other controls, **2 change**. Every step-1 exchange-rate and step-2 PIN message routes exactly as before. Command: `final3.py` in the scratchpad.

**→ What changed.** Only two hidden units (361, 391), both contributing under 0.001 to any logit before. They form one clipped step: **eligibility content on the account_security vector → that logit +3**. The direction is a whitened difference of means from 60 eligibility messages I wrote against 253 generic ones. No fitting to the evidence labels. Shapes, keys, dtypes and all earlier units are identical to the input.

**→ Flag, not fixed.** Step 1's unit 38 is an **unclipped ramp**. It adds up to **+70** to account_security on identity-verification messages and +10 to +24 on fee messages. On my 502 messages it never flips a routing, because it only amplifies an option that already wins. I left it, since step 3 must route "exactly as scorer_in" elsewhere, and changing it would alter that reference.

**→ Mistake: Guard.** Mistake: step 1 shipped an unbounded unit and no step audited per-unit output magnitudes. Guard: `probe.py` now reports min, max and over-gain counts for every edited unit, and the memory note says to run it before accepting any file.

**→ Risk.** Recall on short fragments and on "can I get a card in country X" phrasings is the weak spot. Collateral is estimated on about 300 messages, so the true rate on 3,080 could be 1 to 2%. I did not post to the work board, as this was a single-turn harness task.
